      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s024-p00222",
      "source_en": "This however does not exclude an evolution in the Round Head artistic tradition. Hachid (1998) states that there was an ancient and a final phase, and between them there were numerous different stages which might have been used and reused during the whole period. According to Hachid (1998: 179), who's views this author supports, it is not fundamental to determine the chronological sequences of the styles in such a homogeneous artistic tradition.",
